
---
# yaw, pitch and roll are in DEGREES, from the BNO055 Euler output. pitch has the Python node's
# pitch_offset (degrees) already added. The sign convention of pitch (which way is positive) is NOT
# established anywhere in this repo; do not assume one.
float64 yaw
float64 pitch
float64 roll
# Pitch RATE in DEGREES PER SECOND, from the BNO055 gyroscope (not differentiated from the angle),
# for the pitch controller's D term (finding H-6). Meant to have the SAME sign as pitch: positive
# while pitch is increasing. Which gyro axis is pitch, and its sign, are node parameters that are
# UNVERIFIED until someone tilts the robot (ICM20948.py, pitch_rate_axis / pitch_rate_sign).
# NaN when this cycle's gyro read failed, INDEPENDENTLY of `success`: check it on its own.
float64 pitch_rate_deg_s
# true only if all three ANGLES above come from one good sensor read. It says nothing about
# pitch_rate_deg_s. false means the angle read failed: yaw/pitch/roll are NaN and must be ignored.
bool success
